I have to get two of these in one dress.

347
00:15:40,900 --> 00:15:42,328
女士 请问你有鞋拔子吗
Miss, do you have a shoehorn?

348
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:52,200
快出来 香奈儿的鞋
Come on, Chanel shoes!

349
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:55,340
快出来 山寨香奈儿
Come on, Chanel knockoffs.

350
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:58,400
你怎么还不换衣服
Why are you not dressed yet?

351
00:15:58,740 --> 00:16:00,060
因为女人上厕所慢死了
'Cause ladies take forever.

352
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:01,800
都怪那些塑身裤
It's all the spanx.

353
00:16:02,940 --> 00:16:05,500
去 用我那间 我要伸个头出去
Well, go, use my stall. I want to go stick my head out,

354
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:06,640
看看能不能发现强尼
and see if I can scope out Johnny.

355
00:16:08,231 --> 00:16:11,180
不 女士 不 这不公平
No, ma'am, no! Not fair, ma'am.

356
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:12,980
试试残疾人厕所 这边
Try the handicapper. This side.

357
00:16:13,060 --> 00:16:13,560
好主意
Good idea.

358
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:17,080
我今晚真是霉运不断
I cannot get a break tonight.

359
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:24,280
-麦克斯 -强尼
- Psst, yo, Max. - Johnny!

360
00:16:25,580 --> 00:16:26,476
你在找谁
Who are you looking for?

361
00:16:26,476 --> 00:16:28,597
达美乐披萨仔
The Dominos guy.

362
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:30,460
我躲在里面是因为再过五分钟
I was hiding in there, 'cause five more minutes,

363
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:31,140
披萨就能免费吃
the pizza's free.

364
00:16:32,340 --> 00:16:33,940
我还期待能遇见你呢
I was hoping I'd run into you.

365
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:35,160
也没什么好见的
Eh, no big deal.

366
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:37,720
当然不是 你看起美呆了
Pretty big deal. You look amazing.

367
00:16:38,260 --> 00:16:40,580
美得我蛋疼菊紧 虎躯一震
Amazing. I will go as far as amaze-balls.

368
00:16:42,020 --> 00:16:42,440
多谢夸奖
Thanks.

369
00:16:43,220 --> 00:16:44,620
你看起像广告里那种
You look like a guy in a commercial

370
00:16:44,620 --> 00:16:46,280
藏着戒指和小狗的男人
who has a ring and puppy hidden somewhere.

371
00:16:47,940 --> 00:16:48,960
你能相信吗
Can you believe it?

372
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:50,536
咱俩身穿锦衣华服
We're both at this shmancy thing.

373
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:51,780
我们变化真大呀
Look how far we've gotten.

374
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:54,920
其实当你静心一想
Actually, when you think about it,

375
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:56,180
你会发现我们都没变
we didn't get very far at all.

376
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:00,420
对 你说得对 的确没变
Nope, you're right. We didn't.

377
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:02,380
为什么
Yeah, why?

378
00:17:05,260 --> 00:17:06,360
时机不对吧
Timing, I guess.

379
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:08,100
时机
Timing?

380
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,300
随你怎么说吧
Okay, whatever.

381
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:14,780
从现在开始 每当我想起你
You know, from now on, when I think of you,

382
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:17,260
我会想着你身穿礼服 而不是制服的样子
I'm gonna think of you in this and not the uniform.

383
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:21,620
从现在开始
You know, from now on,

384
00:17:21,620 --> 00:17:23,200
或许你就不该再想我
maybe you shouldn't think of me at all.

385
00:17:25,360 --> 00:17:26,720
走啦 曼哈顿先生
Gotta go, Mr. Manhattan.

386
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:33,400
太棒了 卡洛琳 你在哪里
That was awesome! Caroline, where are you?

387
00:17:33,580 --> 00:17:34,520
我快穿好了
I'm almost dressed.

388
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:38,800
我刚跟强尼来了次完美的当面告别
I just had the perfect in-your-face good-bye with Johnny.

389
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:41,080
说到"当面"
And speaking of "in your face,"

390
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:43,400
他当着我的面 还直勾勾盯着我的胸
he couldn't take his eyes off my boobs...

391
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,540
谁让他要结婚
Boobs that he can never have,

392
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:47,100
这对美胸从此跟他告别了
now that he's getting married.

393
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:53,240
靠 妹子 你真美 你晚点有活动吗
Damn, girl, you look good. What you doing later?

394
00:17:53,600 --> 00:17:54,160
能给我你的电话吗
Can I get your number?

395
00:17:59,180 --> 00:18:03,060
天啊 小蛋糕在我的包包有点被砸碎了
Oh, no, the cupcake got a little smushed in my purse.

396
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:05,660
我们不能拿给玛莎·斯图尔特了
We can't show this to Martha Stewart now.

397
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:06,220
干嘛不可以
Sure, we can.

398
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:08,120
你觉得她没被人用蛋糕糊过脸吗
You think she never had a cupcake smush on her?

399
00:18:08,220 --> 00:18:09,860
我觉得没有
I doubt that very much.

400
00:18:09,940 --> 00:18:11,380
玛莎·斯图尔特是个完人
Martha Stewart is perfect.

401
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:13,140
超凡脱俗 脚不着地
Her feet don't even touch the ground.

402
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:15,420
可能连厕所都不需要上
The woman probably doesn't even go to the bathroom.

403
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:20,980
人无完人
Martha Stewart's hardly perfect.

404
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:22,880
今晚过得好吗
And how are you this evening?

405
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:25,740
你说得对 人无完人 她也不例外
No, you're right, Martha Stewart isn't perfect.

406
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:27,420
这话我可没说过
Oh, I never said that!

407
00:18:28,740 --> 00:18:30,500
其实我听说她超爱虐男人的
In fact, I hear she's a real ballbuster.

408
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:32,820
你什么都没听见
You did not hear that.

409
00:18:32,860 --> 00:18:35,040
真的 超爱虐男人 你知道吗
Yep, a real ballbuster, you know?

410
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:36,280
我什么都不知道
No, I do not know.

411
00:18:37,060 --> 00:18:38,780
能递块毛巾给我吗
Would you mind handing me a towelette please?

412
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:43,560
一块就行 谢谢
Oh, one's fine. Thank you so much.

413
00:18:43,900 --> 00:18:46,560
但就是因为玛莎·斯图尔特那么强悍
But the fact that Martha Stewart is so tough...

414
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:48,420
卡洛琳 你得马上出来
Caroline, you need to get out here right now.

415
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:50,380
那么爱虐男人
The fact that she is a real ballbuster...

416
00:18:51,620 --> 00:18:52,840
神啊 救救我吧
Oh, dear God, help me.

417
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:55,100
所以我才那么喜欢她和敬重她
Is what I like and respect about her.

418
00:18:55,120 --> 00:18:56,580
那个女人是个天才
I mean, the woman's a genius.

419
00:18:56,840 --> 00:18:58,060
越来越有意思了
Now it's getting interesting.

420
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,780
而且 你不能听信传闻
And besides, you can't really believe gossip.

421
00:19:00,900 --> 00:19:02,060
瞧瞧我收到的仇恨信
Look at all that hate mail I got

422
00:19:02,060 --> 00:19:03,400
多少人骂我贱货啊
with people calling me a bitch,

423
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:04,500
可其实我不是
and I'm not a bitch.

424
00:19:04,980 --> 00:19:06,240
这有待商议
Well, that's debatable.

425
00:19:08,420 --> 00:19:10,480
-玛莎·斯图尔特 你好 -你好啊
- Martha Stewart, hi. - Hello.

426
00:19:11,180 --> 00:19:13,620
我是卡洛琳 这是我的生意伙伴麦克斯
I'm Caroline, and this is my business partner, Max,

427
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:15,120
我们的小蛋糕生意刚起步
and we have a start-up cupcake business.

428
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:17,460
妹子 你不是吧 都这样了你还不放手啊
Dude, are you serious? You're still going for it.

429
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:19,660
我知道这非常不合时宜
I know this is highly inappropriate,

430
00:19:19,660 --> 00:19:21,380
但我们今晚带了个小蛋糕过来
but we brought a cupcake here tonight

431
00:19:21,380 --> 00:19:22,880
衷心希望你能尝一口
in hopes that you might taste it.

432
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:25,380
所以你要我在女厕所
So you want me to taste your cupcake

433
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:26,240
吃你的小蛋糕
in the ladies room.

434
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:27,660
还有比这更不合时宜的吗
What's inappropriate about that?

435
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:31,060
我们的生意刚起步 不抓住机会不行啊
We're a start-up business. We've got to take risks.

436
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:32,500
这位是麦克斯 她是烘培师
This is Max. She's the baker.

437
00:19:32,740 --> 00:19:34,800
-你是烘培师啊 -我是烘培师
- You're the baker. - I'm the baker.

438
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:37,600
看起来蛮吸引人的
Hm, it looks quite appealing.

439
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:39,160
天啊
Oh, my God.

440
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:41,760
我知道这是社交场合
I know this is a social event,

441
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:43,820
很抱歉把它弄得那么商业化
so I'm so sorry for making it about business.

442
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:45,420
当你自己出来打拼事业时
When you're in business for yourself,

443
00:19:45,420 --> 00:19:47,020
你必须得把每一个场合
you have to take every situation

444
00:19:47,020 --> 00:19:49,000
都当作是商机
as a business opportunity.

445
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:51,820
瞧 我还随身带着五本书呢
Look, I have five of these in here.

446
00:19:54,120 --> 00:19:55,960
我超爱看你的家政杂志
I love your magazine.

447
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:57,820
我阅读上面每一篇文章
I read every single issue

448
00:19:57,820 --> 00:19:59,800
直到我被抓到不是看病 只是去偷看杂志
until they realized I didn't even go to that doctor.

449
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:03,180
我要说一句
Well, in spite of the fact

450
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:05,180
你至今还没有洗手
that you have not yet washed your hands...

451
00:20:05,400 --> 00:20:07,000
我刚是在里面换衣服的
I was just changing my dress in there.

452
00:20:07,060 --> 00:20:08,780
-我会尝一口 -真的吗
- I'll taste it. - You will?

453
00:20:09,060 --> 00:20:10,920
我喜欢你的闯劲
I like your entrepreneurial drive.

454
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:13,900
而且我深深地觉得
And I have a feeling that it's actually

455
00:20:13,900 --> 00:20:15,520
只有尝一口 才能活着离开这儿
the only way I'm gonna get out of here alive.

456
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:19,640
这是我们的酒混面粉加枫蜜培根的
That is our beer batter maple bacon

457
00:20:19,640 --> 00:20:20,800
特制春假小蛋糕
spring break cupcake.

458
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:22,900
-名字不错 -谢谢
- Hm, clever name. - Thank you.

459
00:20:23,120 --> 00:20:25,080
不过有点糊了 真可惜
It is a little smushed, though. That's unfortunate.

460
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:26,310
我都说了
I told you.

461
00:20:31,046 --> 00:20:33,367
蛮好吃的
Mmm. Quiet tasty.

462
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:34,960
我喜欢
I like it.

463
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:36,840
你们有名片吗
Do you girls have a card?

464
00:20:39,020 --> 00:20:40,020
拿出来 拿出来 快拿出来
Get it out, get it out, get it out.

465
00:20:42,360 --> 00:20:44,099
非常感谢
Ah, thank you very much.

466
00:20:44,099 --> 00:20:46,222
"麦克斯自制小蛋糕"
"Max's homemade cupcakes."

467
00:20:47,620 --> 00:20:49,920
你知道谁会超级喜欢你们的小蛋糕吗
Well, you know who'd really like that cupcake?

468
00:20:50,820 --> 00:20:51,420
瘾君子
Stoners.

469
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:56,400
她念了"麦克斯自制小蛋糕"这名字
She said "Max's homemade cupcakes."

470
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:58,780
玛莎·斯图尔特喜欢我们的小蛋糕
Martha Stewart likes our cupcakes!

471
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:02,300
玛莎·斯图尔特喜欢我们的小蛋糕
Martha Stewart likes our cupcakes!
